// The loop of ode_utf8, at the first instruction of its body: i bytes are looked at and hold `count` code
// points, and what the bytes from i on add to that count is the whole count (or fails as the whole does).
// In the stack: [0] c, [8] need, [16] state.
place +0x74 {
    name i = r12
    name count = r13
    name state = stack[16]
    fact state == 0
    fact i <= n
    fact count <= i
    fact points(input, i, count) == utf8(input)
    any r14, r15, stack[0], stack[8]
    decreases n - i
}
